-- title:
--   Extra variables preserve unique expressibility in u
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative ring, and $X$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of the project's kind over $B$, of which only its underlying two-variable formal group law $F = X.F$ enters; let $I$ be an ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ and let $u = (u_1,u_2)$ be a pair of elements of $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ with $\mathrm{constantCoeff}(u_j)=0$ for both $j$. Writing $x=(x_1,x_2)$ and $y=(y_1,y_2)$ for the two summands of $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,2$, assume: for every $w \in B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ such that $w(F(x,y)) - w(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under $x \mapsto y$, there is a unique $W \in B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ with $W(u_1,u_2) = w$. The conclusion is the same assertion with arbitrarily many further variables adjoined: for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and every $w \in B[\![x_1,x_2,t_1,\dots,t_n]\!]$ such that $w(F(x,y),t) - w(x,t)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y,t]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under $x \mapsto y$, there is a unique $W \in B[\![x_1,x_2,t_1,\dots,t_n]\!]$ with $W(u_1(x),u_2(x),t) = w$, all substitutions being the ones that leave the variables $t$ fixed.
--
--   This is the bootstrap step from the one-block case to the case with extra parameters in the construction of isogenies of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules out of invariant coordinates, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_existsUnique_subst_of_invariant_of_forall_existsUnique_subst.lean

